lines+=['','Before R48, A live durations are q1:5, q14:7, q8:7, q9:8, q2:6, q16:4, q15:7 steps. Preparation has 12 idle qubit-steps: q9 contributes 5, q15 3, q16 2, q1/q14 1 each. Data q10/q3 have their last pre-round CX/reset/measurement at step 32; q10 still receives T-dagger at 33 and its long idle gap is 34–47. q10 waiting Z/Y faults paired with late A encoder faults dominate the A-CX cross term. Full channel provenance and top pairs: `a30/attribution_verified.json`.','','## Mechanisms and scope','','The initial SAT improvement traded a slightly larger second-order term for a smaller normalized cubic term. Commuting CX reorderings, q14 input reuse and the selected checks then reduced loss further. The final FAST variant advances 2→8, delays 9→8, and retains q2’s reset. This changes fault propagation and exposure without adding CX or delaying the round. CX count and depth are not the objective. An encoder-only Pauli-class calculation moves three potential weight-two-Z partner classes from data20 to four on data7, while retaining four on data10 and three on data0. The count rises from 10 to 11 even though full-circuit loss falls; that surrogate omits the exterior, C17 coupling and conditioning. Details are in a30/fault_class_mechanism.json.','', 'Post-round parity checks lose because the judge adds trailing idle noise to unmeasured data until the last ancilla operation; best tested cubic loss is 2.61618e-4. Internal flag windows either fail to fit or add enough cost to lose their benefit; best floor-passing cubic loss is 7.43117e-5. All 50 valid staggered A-coupling variants failed to improve loss: shorter exposure alone does not preserve error-detection timing.','', 'With B/C and data endpoints fixed, exhaustive nearest-neighbor matching yields exactly one stationary A placement: [1,14,8,9,2,16,15]. There is no A-to-unused-cell edge. The 120 free-cell transports use both exact libraries and all 30 code classes on the connected staging sets; 118 have vanishing c1. Their R spans 102–162 and exp(-A1) spans 0.0212–0.0996. This rules out this endpoint-swap family, not arbitrary interleaved routing or borrowed B/C helpers.','','## Speed exclusions\n\nThe lowest cubic candidate a30_fbn_08352 has cubic 5.72978467582e-5 and all-orders 5.79840882718e-5, but XTIM measured 180.0 s/1e6 (SLOW). Its MC was terminated by verified host PID before any 1e8 seed completed; unchanged exact2 was allowed to finish. A nearby q2-reuse variant was also SLOW at 146.1 s/1e6. Moving data20’s final T-dagger from step 47 to 40 preserved cubic loss but remained SLOW (127.2 s/1e6); that edit is rejected and absent from the winner. Twelve best candidates retaining q2’s reset were FAST on owl; finalists were retimed on zebra. The predictor was copied byte-identically into BCFB because owl lacked XTIM’s file.\n\n## Verified versus inferred','','Verified: target stabilizers and deterministic flags, exact native folding and times, full-circuit correctness construction, the 14 reference ablations, unchanged exact2 CLI, judge, XTIM and MC receipts for the retained finalists, and all-orders 72/canonical scope assertions. The sparse evaluator is byte-identical to the source snapshot; only its location changed because its CLI writes beside itself. No judge or evaluator arithmetic was edited.','', 'Not proved: global A optimality, arbitrary helper instruments, arbitrary moving placements, or that the remaining gap to the leader is unavoidable. The search counts are finite coverage, not exhaustive synthesis. Prior v25k/v26n work was cancelled by MAIN and was not resumed; its evidence is in `REPORT_v25_v26_cancelled.md`.','']
